.Dd August 21, 2026
.Dt WHOIS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm whois
.Nd Internet domain name and network number directory service
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl \-debug
.Op Fl \-help|\-?
.Op Fl \-version
.Op Fl @|\-\-auto
.Op Fl a|\-\-arin
.Op Fl A|\-\-apnic
.Op Fl b|\-\-abuse
.Op Fl c|\-\-tld|\-\-country Ar TLD
.Op Fl d|\-\-db|\-\-database Ar DIR
.Op Fl D|\-\-nodb
.Op Fl f|\-\-afrinic
.Op Fl F|\-\-force
.Op Fl g|\-\-gov
.Op Fl h|\-\-host Ar HOST
.Op Fl i|\-\-internic
.Op Fl I|\-\-iana
.Op Fl k|\-\-kisa|\-\-krnic
.Op Fl l|\-\-lacnic
.Op Fl m|\-\-ra|\-\-radb
.Op Fl p|\-\-port Ar PORT
.Op Fl q|\-\-quiet
.Op Fl P|\-\-peering
.Op Fl Q|\-\-quick
.Op Fl r|\-\-ripe
.Op Fl R|\-\-recursive
.Op Fl S|\-\-verbatim
.Op Fl \-
.Ar simple_query|'complex query' ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility looks up records in the databases maintained by several Network Information Centers
.Pq Tn NICs .
.Pp
By default
.Nm
starts by querying the Internet Assigned Numbers Authority
.Pq Tn IANA
whois server, and follows referrals to whois servers that have more specific details about the
.Ar query .
The
.Tn IANA
whois server knows about IP address and AS numbers as well as domain names.
.Pp
However, when the query is about an IP address, this
.Nm
version will directly goes to the appropriate registry server,
as well as automatically following to the relevant registry server when the
.Tn ARIN
registry points to another registry without issuing a redirection.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Ss OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl h|\-\-host Ar HOST
Use the specified
.Ar HOST
instead of the default.
Either a host name or an IP address may be specified.
.It Fl p|\-\-port Ar PORT
Connect to the whois server on
.Ar PORT .
If this option is not specified,
.Nm
defaults to port 43.
.It Fl Q|\-\-quick
Do a quick lookup;
.Nm
will not attempt to follow referrals to other whois servers.
This is the default if a server is explicitly specified
using one of the other options or in an environment variable.
See also the
.Fl R
option.
.It Fl R|\-\-recursive
Do a recursive lookup;
.Nm
will attempt to follow referrals to other whois servers.
This is the default if no server is explicitly specified.
See also the
.Fl Q
option.
.It Fl S|\-\-verbatim
By default
.Nm
adjusts simple queries (without spaces) to produce more useful output from certain whois servers,
and it suppresses some uninformative output.
With the
.Fl S
option,
.Nm
sends the query and prints the output verbatim.
.It Fl q|\-\-quiet
Hide comments
.It Fl @|\-\-auto
Tell which server would be selected and abort the query
.It Fl a|\-\-arin
Use the American Registry for Internet Numbers
.Pq Tn ARIN
database.
It contains network numbers used in those parts of the world covered neither by
.Tn APNIC , AfriNIC , LACNIC ,
nor by
.Tn RIPE .
The query syntax is documented at
.Pa https://www.arin.net/resources/registry/whois/rws/cli/
.It Fl A|\-\-apnic
Use the Asia/Pacific Network Information Center
.Pq Tn APNIC
database.
It contains network numbers used in East Asia, Australia, New Zealand, and the Pacific islands.
The query syntax is documented at
.Pa https://www.apnic.net/manage\-ip/using\-whois/searching/query\-options/
or you can get it using
.Ic whois \-A help
.It Fl b|\-\-abuse
Use the Network Abuse Clearinghouse database.
It contains addresses to which network abuse should be reported, indexed by domain name.
.It Fl c|\-\-tld|\-\-country Ar TLD
This is the equivalent of using the
.Fl h
option with an argument of
.Qq Ar TLD Ns Li .whois\-servers.net .
This can be helpful for locating country\-class TLD whois servers.
.It Fl f|\-\-afrinic
Use the African Network Information Centre
.Pq Tn AfriNIC
database.
It contains network numbers used in Africa and the islands of the western Indian Ocean.
The query syntax was documented at
https://www.afrinic.net/support/whois/manual
or you can get it using
.Ic whois \-f help
.It Fl g|\-\-gov
Use the US non\-military federal government database, which contains points of contact for subdomains of
.Pa .GOV .
.It Fl i|\-\-internic
Use the traditional Network Information Center
.Pq Tn InterNIC
.Pq Pa whois.internic.net
database.
This now contains only registrations for domain names under
.Pa .COM ,
.Pa .NET ,
.Pa .EDU .
You can specify the type of object to search for like
.Ic whois \-i ' Ns Ar type Ar name Ns Ic '
where
.Ar type
can be
.Nm domain , nameserver , registrar .
The
.Ar name
can contain
.Li *
wildcards.
Get query syntax documentation using
.Ic whois \-i help
.It Fl I|\-\-iana
Use the Internet Assigned Numbers Authority
.Pq Tn IANA
database.
The query syntax is documented at
.Pa https://www.iana.org/help/whois
.It Fl k|\-\-kisa|\-\-krnic
Use the National Internet Development Agency of Korea’s
.Pq Tn KRNIC
database.
It contains network numbers and domain contact information for Korea.
.It Fl l|\-\-lacnic
Use the Latin American and Caribbean IP address Regional Registry
.Pq Tn LACNIC
database.
This server accepts only direct match queries (POCs, ownerid, CIDR blocks, IP and AS numbers).
.It Fl m|\-\-ra|\-\-radb
Use the Route Arbiter Database
.Pq Tn RADB
database.
It contains route policy specifications for a large number of operators’ networks.
.It Fl P|\-\-peering
Use the PeeringDB database of AS numbers.
It contains details about presence at internet peering points for many network operators.
.It Fl r|\-\-ripe
Use the R\(aaeseaux IP Europ\(aaeens
.Pq Tn RIPE
database.
It contains network numbers and domain contact information for Europe.
The query syntax is documented at
https://docs.db.ripe.net/Tables\-of\-Query\-Types\-Supported\-by\-the\-RIPE\-Database
or you can get it using
.Ic whois \-r help
.It Fl d|\-\-db|\-\-database Ar DIR
Use the
.Ar DIR
directory as WHOIS cache database
.It Fl D|\-\-nodb
Don't use the environment defined cache database
.It Fl F|\-\-force
Force a refresh of the WHOIS cache for the queries
.It Fl \-debug
Enable debug mode
.It Fl \-help|\-?
Print usage and this help message and exit
.It Fl \-version
Print version and exit
.It Fl -
Options processing terminator.
Specific WHOIS server options can be used after
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
The
.Ev WHOIS_DEBUG
environment variable can be set to any value to enable debug mode.
.Pp
The
.Ev FLAVOUR
or
.Ev WHOIS_FLAVOUR
environment variables can be set to one of the following values, to implement only the corresponding options and behaviours:
.Bl -bullet
.It
bsd | bsd:freebsd : FreeBSD whois(1)
.El
.Pp
Other classical environment variables:
.Bl -tag -width WHOIS_SERVER
.It Ev WHOIS_SERVER
The primary default whois server.
If this is unset,
.Nm
uses the
.Ev RA_SERVER
environment variable.
.It Ev RA_SERVER
The secondary default whois server.
If this is unset,
.Nm
will use
.Pa whois.iana.org
or auto\-select the server for IP addresses.
.El
.Pp
Version specific environment variables:
.Bl -tag -width WHOIS_CACHEDAYS
.It Ev WHOIS_DATABASE
A directory pathname where the compressed query results will be stored
.It Ev WHOIS_CACHEDAYS
An integer specifying the number of days a cached result can be reused
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
To obtain contact information about an
administrator located in the Russian
.Tn TLD
domain
.Qq Li RU ,
use the
.Fl c
option as shown in the following example, where
.Ar CONTACT\-ID
is substituted with the actual contact identifier.
.Pp
.Dl Ic whois \-c RU CONTACT\-ID
.Pp
(Note: This example is specific to the
.Tn TLD
.Qq Li RU ,
but other
.Tn TLDs
can be queried by using a similar syntax.)
.Pp
The following example demonstrates how to query
a whois server using a non-standard port, where
.Dq Li query\-data
is the query to be sent to
.Dq Li whois.example.com
on port
.Dq Li rwhois
(written numerically as 4321).
.Pp
.Dl Ic whois \-h whois.example.com \-p rwhois query\-data
.Pp
Some whois servers support complex queries
with dash\-letter options.
You can use the
.Fl -
option to separate
.Nm
command options from whois server query options.
A query containing spaces must be quoted as one
argument to the
.Nm
command.
The following example asks the RIPE whois server
to return a brief description of its
.Dq Li domain
object type:
.Pp
.Dl Ic whois \-r \-\- '\-t domain'
